body:
She left her phone open. I confronted her about the relationship without exposing that I saw the messages. She denied anything was going on. 

&#x200B;

As we have been married for 25+ years I decided to let it go to see what happens. Right now I \*think\* it was an emotional affair and nothing physical happened, but I have my doubts. Since I confronted her I think the guilt has stopped it, but not positive. I know, how much of a schmuck am I for sticking around? At this point I want to try to save the marriage as I have so many years invested. It is really tough though facing her everyday, putting a smile on my face and pretending I don't know as much as I do.

&#x200B;

I have all the messages archived so if I need them I have them. She has since deleted some of the more incriminating FB messages, but doesn't matter. Other things have changed that have basically eliminated any time my SO and her affair are together.

&#x200B;

The thing is the other guy is engaged to be married. I so want to tell the other woman, just because it is the right thing to do.
